hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan today I'm  answering the question from one of my  readers Bashir who wrote in with a  question about franchising so he said  your personal opinion regards to  franchising as a tool to grow as well as  franchise and advantages and risks so  thanks for the question Bashir  franchising can be a great way to grow  your business it really depends on the  company that you're running franchising  is a great way to grow quickly because  you're not using your own money to  expand you're using your franchisees who  have to invest capital to buy your  franchise and it's to be a quick way to  rapidly grow at your business some of  the things to think about with  franchising first you have to have a  really successful location yourself and  a lot of people try to franchise too  early they franchise with just an idea  and they haven't really proven it  themselves too much and then if you  haven't built a successful business  yourself with your first location it's  gonna be really hard to have other  people be successful because they're  gonna be copying your model and if your  model isn't bulletproof and works  amazingly well then it's not going to  work for somebody else and you have to  remember that the franchisees are  probably not going to be as successful  as you are so whatever your first  location is that's gonna be probably the  most successful location in the system  until you maybe move into bigger markets  but it has to work and a lot of  entrepreneurs is franchise  too soon so make sure you have one  really successful location you can bring  people to you can show them how it works  and it's an easy way to give an  incentive for somebody to want to look  at that one location say hey I can do  this and I can make a lot of money as  well so it has to be highly profitable  before you think about expansion the  next thing to think about is you have to  really have everything documented so  it's a lot of work on your part you got  to figure out for each new location  here's exactly what you have to do to be  successful and again remember that the  franchisees are not going to do  everything exactly as you say unless you  specifically lay it out so they're not  going to think the same way as you think  so you have to really be specific as to  what they have to do and do that  every step and so it's a lot of work  creating the paperwork to have all that  put together and then the final thing to  think about with franchising is a lot of  entrepreneurs who go that route you find  that most of your time is spent no  longer running the business but managing  the franchisees and you have to do a  good job at the beginning to qualify  your franchisees and make sure bringing  the right people on board so you're not  just bringing somebody on because they  have the money to do it you want  somebody who you've done interviews with  and you feel they're in the right stage  of life to do it they have the right  experience to do it they're willing to  listen to your advice on how to keep  going and if you get the wrong person  you're gonna spend too much of your time  just managing that person and they're  not gonna see success and you're not  going to see success you're both just  gonna have a miserable time so you have  to think do you want to be in that  business of just managing franchisees  because that's what you're gonna end up  doing right so you have your one  location and you might even open a few  more yourself and most of your time is  gonna be spent managing your franchisees  and a lot of entrepreneur friends of  mine didn't expect that and they ended  up either closing down a lot of the  franchisees or taking them over again so  they could just be the entrepreneur and  not have to worry about other people  owning operating it so the the biggest  Pro is that you are able to expand very  quickly using other people's money you  don't need to go out and raise capital  you don't have the money yourself  necessarily yet because you're you're  trying to go through the your profits  originally so using other people's money  to quickly expand the business you get  more branding that the cons are you know  the you have to manage all these  franchisees ongoing nobody's gonna run  it as as good as you do and yeah you  basically are running this organization  that you don't have full control of  anymore so a lot of people don't like  the franchising model I think it's a  tracted from the beginning but once they  get into it they thought they're into  kind of completely different world I  would I would suggest if you're still  interested in doing it going to talk to  people who have done the franchises and  I talk to franchisees and I try to talk  to the franchise owners as well don't go  up and talk to somebody from McDonald's  but find a smaller franchisee somebody  who might be in a  similar type of business to what you're  trying to do and just get their  experiences and thoughts and see if  that's something that you still want to  do or not so hopefully that helped  thanks for the question it's it's always  good to try to get as much knowledge as  you can about something before you jump  into it if you guys like the video who  are watching please give it a thumbs up  below  it makes gonna do more for you and if  you have a comment about this video or  you have a question for your own  business I'd love to hear from you if  you want to leave it in the comment  section below so thank you and I'll see  you on the next episode  you
 

